WEBVTT

00:00:00.594 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.895 --> 00:00:06.270
Today it is lash lifting and tinting, usually just called a lash lift.

00:00:06.779 --> 00:00:09.710
Unlike extensions, no lashes are added here.

00:00:10.134 --> 00:00:14.670
We curl the client's own natural lashes, then tint them so they look darker.

00:00:15.131 --> 00:00:17.070
The result is soft and natural.

00:00:17.576 --> 00:00:20.570
But because we use chemicals, right next to the eye,

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.590
acting directly on the natural lash, we have to understand it properly.

00:00:25.187 --> 00:00:28.029
Put simply, a lash lift has three parts.

00:00:28.355 --> 00:00:33.629
First, the lashes are brushed up onto a small silicone shield, stuck on the eyelid.

00:00:34.044 --> 00:00:37.907
Second, the first lotion softens the inner structure of the lash,

00:00:37.857 --> 00:00:40.429
so it takes on the new shape of the shield.

00:00:40.846 --> 00:00:43.629
Third, the second lotion sets that shape.

00:00:43.965 --> 00:00:46.749
Released from the shield, the lashes keep their curl.

00:00:47.357 --> 00:00:48.827
Who does a lash lift suit?

00:00:49.317 --> 00:00:53.531
Usually clients whose natural lashes are fairly long but grow straight,

00:00:53.481 --> 00:00:54.587
or point downward,

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:57.787
who do not want extensions, or want less upkeep.

00:00:58.295 --> 00:01:02.107
Very short lashes are hard to lift nicely, so tell the client beforehand.

00:01:02.456 --> 00:01:05.743
And a client who has extensions must have them removed first,

00:01:05.693 --> 00:01:07.707
as in the refills and removal lesson.

00:01:08.056 --> 00:01:10.587
Never lift lashes that still have extensions on them.

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:13.083
How long does each lotion stay on?

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.403
There is no single number for everyone.

00:01:15.504 --> 00:01:17.003
It depends on the lash type:

00:01:17.105 --> 00:01:19.963
fine, normal, or thick and coarse.

00:01:20.311 --> 00:01:21.803
And it depends on the product.

00:01:22.076 --> 00:01:26.843
Fine lashes usually need less time, thick, coarse lashes need longer.

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:29.163
Each brand has its own timing chart.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:31.798
Always follow the instructions of the brand,

00:01:31.748 --> 00:01:34.683
and look closely at the client's lashes before you choose.

00:01:35.346 --> 00:01:39.334
Choose the shield by the length of the lashes, and the curl the client wants.

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:43.413
Short lashes take a small shield, long lashes a larger one.

00:01:43.674 --> 00:01:47.576
For the same lash length, a smaller shield gives a stronger curl,

00:01:47.526 --> 00:01:49.414
a larger shield gives a softer,

00:01:49.455 --> 00:01:50.374
gentler curl.

00:01:50.925 --> 00:01:54.214
A shield that is too small for the lashes makes them curl over.

00:01:54.508 --> 00:01:58.934
Too large, and the lashes are only slightly lifted, with little visible difference.

00:01:59.051 --> 00:02:01.974
And the position of the shield matters as much as its size.

00:02:02.215 --> 00:02:04.454
The shield must sit right against the lash line.

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:08.081
If it sits away from the lash line, the root is not lifted,

00:02:08.031 --> 00:02:11.254
and the lash gets a kink in the middle that looks very odd.

00:02:11.875 --> 00:02:13.671
Here is something that happens a lot.

00:02:14.098 --> 00:02:16.194
The client wants really curly lashes,

00:02:16.144 --> 00:02:19.511
so the technician leaves the lotion on a few minutes longer,

00:02:19.556 --> 00:02:20.471
just to be sure.

00:02:20.895 --> 00:02:23.191
Or chooses a shield that is too small.

00:02:23.525 --> 00:02:24.151
The result:

00:02:24.499 --> 00:02:29.991
lashes that are frizzy, curled too tight, dry and brittle, with some broken off.

00:02:30.498 --> 00:02:33.985
Because the lotion acts on the structure of the lash itself,

00:02:33.935 --> 00:02:36.391
leaving it on too long damages the lashes.

00:02:36.492 --> 00:02:38.311
And it cannot be fixed right away:

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:40.791
you have to wait for new lashes to grow.

00:02:41.181 --> 00:02:45.431
Lifting again too soon, before the lashes have recovered, does the same.

00:02:45.857 --> 00:02:49.511
For the gap between two lifts, follow the instructions of the brand.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:51.280
Now the tint.

00:02:51.846 --> 00:02:56.650
Lash and brow tint is a separate product, mixed exactly as the brand instructs,

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:59.840
and only products made for lashes and brows are used.

00:03:00.266 --> 00:03:02.160
Never use hair dye on lashes.

00:03:02.668 --> 00:03:06.938
The tint is usually mixed just before use, in the exact ratio on the label,

00:03:06.888 --> 00:03:09.920
and applied while the lashes are still on the shield,

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:13.600
after the second lotion, if the instructions of the brand say so too.

00:03:13.942 --> 00:03:18.000
Choose the shade by the client's brow and hair color, so it looks natural.

00:03:18.459 --> 00:03:23.600
In Europe, lash tint labels must carry allergy warnings, under EU rules.

00:03:24.101 --> 00:03:28.080
Every time you change products, read the label and the instructions again.

00:03:28.628 --> 00:03:32.137
Many tint brands require an allergy test before tinting,

00:03:32.087 --> 00:03:34.484
often 48 hours before the appointment.

00:03:34.987 --> 00:03:38.349
Dab a little tint on the area of skin the brand specifies,

00:03:38.299 --> 00:03:41.204
often behind the ear or in the crook of the elbow,

00:03:41.389 --> 00:03:42.004
then wait.

00:03:42.498 --> 00:03:47.044
If there is redness, itching, swelling or burning, do not tint.

00:03:47.473 --> 00:03:49.604
Write the test date in the client's profile.

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.324
Do the test exactly as the product says.

00:03:52.495 --> 00:03:54.821
For the signs of an allergy and what to do,

00:03:54.771 --> 00:03:57.044
see the lesson on allergies and chemicals.

00:03:57.666 --> 00:03:58.898
When not to do it?

00:03:59.233 --> 00:04:03.565
Eyes that are red, inflamed or watering, recent eye surgery,

00:04:03.515 --> 00:04:05.777
irritated skin around the eyes,

00:04:06.043 --> 00:04:08.578
or a past reaction to lift lotion or tint.

00:04:09.005 --> 00:04:12.578
For the full list, see the lesson on when not to do a service.

00:04:13.006 --> 00:04:17.218
If you are not sure, do not do it, and advise the client to ask a doctor.

00:04:17.928 --> 00:04:19.151
An absolute rule:

00:04:19.414 --> 00:04:21.391
the lotion must never get into the eye.

00:04:21.727 --> 00:04:23.871
The client's eyes stay closed throughout.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:27.488
The lift lotion goes only on the lower part of the lash,

00:04:27.438 --> 00:04:30.591
a little away from the skin, never on the eyelid skin,

00:04:30.858 --> 00:04:32.111
and not out to the tips.

00:04:32.465 --> 00:04:34.991
Use very little lotion, so it does not run.

00:04:35.461 --> 00:04:37.231
If lotion does get into the eye:

00:04:37.429 --> 00:04:39.711
rinse at once with plenty of clean water.

00:04:39.944 --> 00:04:45.151
If the eye still hurts, is red, or vision is blurred, see a doctor straight away.

00:04:45.789 --> 00:04:46.695
After the lift,

00:04:46.645 --> 00:04:50.808
tell the client to keep her lashes dry for as long as the brand advises,

00:04:50.758 --> 00:04:51.722
usually one day.

00:04:52.137 --> 00:04:53.162
During that time:

00:04:53.221 --> 00:04:59.162
no mascara, no steam, no rubbing her eyes, and no sleeping face down on the pillow.

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:02.442
After that, brush the lashes gently every day.

00:05:03.092 --> 00:05:04.541
How long does the curl last?

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:08.221
Usually about six to eight weeks, depending on the person.

00:05:08.745 --> 00:05:13.181
Because, as in the classic lesson, natural lashes have a life cycle:

00:05:13.366 --> 00:05:16.461
old lashes fall out, and new ones grow in straight.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:20.141
So the result lasts about as long as the life cycle of a lash.

00:05:20.407 --> 00:05:24.141
Once there are lots of new lashes, it is time for the client to come back.

00:05:24.783 --> 00:05:25.508
So you see.

00:05:25.842 --> 00:05:29.748
A lash lift looks simple, but safety lies in the small details:

00:05:29.856 --> 00:05:33.410
the right shield, the right timing, the lotion in the right place,

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.268
and an allergy test before tinting.

00:05:35.676 --> 00:05:38.308
In the practice lesson, we will go step by step.

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:41.028
And now, take the short quiz below the video.

00:05:41.277 --> 00:05:42.068
See you next time.
